WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.447
This slide focuses on Count values that meet a
condition The goal is to understand

00:00:05.461 --> 00:00:11.719
the idea in plain language before connecting it to
code or analytical use Flagging

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:17.340
pattern A counter can summarize how many
observations match a rule Start the counter

00:00:17.353 --> 00:00:22.924
at 0 Before running the example predict what the
output should

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:28.703
look like Run it in the browser inspect the result
then change one value condition

00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:35.389
or input and run it again Pay attention to what
changed and why Loop

00:00:35.416 --> 00:00:41.076
through each value If the rule is true add 1 Print
the final

00:00:41.102 --> 00:00:41.589
count
